cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CityParquet: a columnar encoding for 3D city models"
message: >-
  If you use CityParquet — the specification, the reference implementation, or
  the benchmark results — please cite this repository.
type: software
authors:
  # Add `orcid: "https://orcid.org/…"` here before the first release.
  - given-names: Hidemichi
    family-names: Baba
    affiliation: "3D Geoinformation, Delft University of Technology"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cityjson/cityparquet"
abstract: >-
  CityParquet is a columnar Parquet encoding for 3D city models. It stores a
  CityJSON / CityGML model as a directory of Parquet files split by CityGML
  module — one row per city object, WKB geometry in a per-LoD column paired with
  a struct carrying the semantics WKB cannot hold, and optional sidecar tables
  for materials, textures and geometry templates — so national-to-global city
  models can be pruned, filtered and queried directly over cloud object storage.
  At LoD0 a CityParquet footprint is conformant GeoParquet. This repository holds
  the normative specification, the Rust reference reader/writer, a DuckDB-based
  lakehouse prototype, and the benchmarks the design is argued from.
keywords:
  - CityJSON
  - CityGML
  - Parquet
  - GeoParquet
  - 3D city models
  - cloud-native geospatial
  - columnar storage
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
